nt":"p.395 - sidebar on Disciplines - 'Endurance' should be 'Stamina'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T15:57:28-08:00","id":1184541,"title":"","content":"p. 370, &quot;Practicing Safe Oblivion&quot; sidebar: &quot;A destructive, treacherous <b>Spectrecharacter</b>...&quot; Missing space.<br /> p. 370, &quot;Practicing Safe Oblivion&quot; sidebar: &quot;Making <i>characters</i> uncomfortable is one thing; making <i>players</i> uncomfortable or feel unwelcome...&quot; Awkward, ungrammatical phrasing. Perhaps &quot;Making <i>characters</i> feel uncomfortable is one thing; making <i>players</i> feel uncomfortable or unwelcome...&quot;<br /> p. 374: Incorrect indentation of the last line of unbulleted text in the &quot;Malfeans&quot; heading.<br /> p. 378, Redemption vs. Redemption sidebar: &quot;Most understand, if don't necessarily agree, with...&quot; Comma should appear after with; awkward phrasing anyhow.<br /> p. 378, Redemption vs. Redemption sidebar: &quot;But just because they believe it exists doesn't mean <b>they're pursue it</b>...&quot; Additionally, awkward phrasing of &quot;...they believe it exists doesn't mean...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13535-leftmost-cat","user":"Leftmost Cat","date":". 02-10-2018, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13535-leftmost-cat","name":"Leftmost Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T16:39:48-08:00","id":1184550,"title":"","content":"p51 &quot;Built largely from long-replaced pieces of Grand Central, Union Station, Gare de Lyon, and many more, it has an immense Victorian grandeur that both welcomes wraiths to the island and warns them that <b>theyshould </b>be on their best behavior.&quot; Missing space.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T16:48:24-08:00","id":1184555,"title":"","content":"P. 395, Risen Discipline use seems to go by the old version of Celerity, which would be more out of place than the alteration to Potence if going by V20, where each action costs a blood point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T17:17:39-08:00","id":1184564,"title":"","content":"p. 406: &quot;The end result, however, is the same, a human who is aware (and occasionally can't get away from) the Restless Dead.&quot; Comma after same should be a colon, should be &quot;aware of&quot;.<br /> p. 408: &quot;Each novizio forges his own, ...&quot; Likely that &quot;<i>novizio</i>&quot; should be italicized.<br /> p. 409: &quot;Humans in the Underworld&quot; sidebar has no space before &quot;Other Awakened&quot; and cuts off immediately after.<br /> p. 422: Under &quot;Mourners&quot;, the &quot;Image:&quot; section is likely meant to be &quot;Description:&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13535-leftmost-cat","user":"Leftmost Cat","date":". 02-10-2018, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13535-leftmost-cat","name":"Leftmost Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T22:31:18-08:00","id":1184632,"title":"","content":"Trait Cost Chart on page 302 lists Merit. No merits or flaws are listed anywhere in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T00:52:22-08:00","id":1184655,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 302: </b>&quot;One <b>Point </b>\u2014 Survival:&quot; -- the word <i>point </i>is lowercase in the other entries","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T05:08:25-08:00","id":1184701,"title":"","content":"Hey folks, can we move anything that isn't a listing of errata to a new thread please? Please don't discuss things here. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T05:25:30-08:00","id":1184704,"title":"","content":"p.296 says fire is soakable with Stamina. It doesn't qualify this to say 'with the use of special Arcanoi'. But p.328 specifically says aggravated damage can only be soaked with Arcanoi etc. If this is an exception, it should be clarified. If the mechanics are supposed to represent dodging the flames instead, then Stamina seems the wrong dice pool (Dexterity + Survival/Athletics would make more sense). This is presumably due to copying-and-pasting from Second Edition (which never actually said aggravated damage was unsoakable anywhere in the text, and was like CTD2e in that respect).<br /> <br /> Perhaps, for clarity, it would also make sense to mention that aggravated damage can't be soaked on p.295 where soaking and damage are first mentioned ('damage...may be bashing, lethal, or aggravated depending on the source. Damage can usually be soaked'). Otherwise, you're searching through another 33 pages to discover that rather important detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T09:02:00-08:00","id":1184754,"title":"","content":"Page 221 &quot;No one else can here its whispered asides&quot; should be &quot; No one else can hear its whispered asides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T09:54:42-08:00","id":1184777,"title":"","content":"Page 481, under Marrow. The Prohibited Arcanos is listed as Sandman instead of Phantasm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T13:15:37-08:00","id":1184857,"title":"","content":"On page 226 &quot;. . . can lead the group into a cycle of escalating Shadow-driven retaliation that can drive the whole off the rails.&quot; I think is meant to say &quot;drive the whole game off the rails.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T13:18:23-08:00","id":1184860,"title":"","content":"Same picture used on pages 223 and 364.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23863,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23863-gothmate","user":"gothmate","date":". 02-11-2018, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23863-gothmate","name":"gothmate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T13:20:34-08:00","id":1184861,"title":"","content":"Shadow Character Sheet doesn't have an Experience points Box.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23863,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23863-gothmate","user":"gothmate","date":". 02-11-2018, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23863-gothmate","name":"gothmate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T14:02:22-08:00","id":1184882,"title":"","content":"On page 231 in the first line for Aura of Corruption, &quot;Thorn \u2018s&quot; has a space before the apostrophe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T14:13:16-08:00","id":1184883,"title":"","content":"1 - The word &quot;System&quot; on page 153 is not in bold.<br /> <br /> As I have read, I see that there are several occurrences of this error. I imagine it would be the case to search CTRL + L for all the entries in this word and to check that all of them are in bold, if any.<br /> <br /> 2 - On the page 331 says (Defensive Maneuvers). A dodge its a Dex + Athletics roll or a Dex + Dodge roll? There is a description to Dodge on Talents. This is correct? All previous 20th editions abolish the Dodge Talent for Athletics one. The Abilities set is crazy.<br /> <br /> 3 - Suggestion. Insert a free blank space on botton Abilities, a 11th one, as V20 and W20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23868-fspardoner","user":"fspardoner","date":".  Updating as I progress in reading. 02-12-2018, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23868-fspardoner","name":"fspardoner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23868_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T14:15:04-08:00","id":1184884,"title":"","content":"Whilst it might be possible I've just overlooked it somewhere despite a pretty deep dig; but I don't seem able to locate any system for Lifesight, Deathsight or Heightened Senses. They are described on page 20 in &quot;Wraith Characteristics&quot; but no system is given.<br /> <br /> There are references in several places to adding to dice pools for Life/Death-sight but not what the dice pool is actually based on.<br /> <br /> Usury - Appraisal page 217<br /> Spectre Characteristics page 348<br /> Risen - Basic Risen/Wraith Abilities, page 395<br /> Projectors - Dead Eyes page 479<br /> <br /> As well as references to Discern Weakness, Sense Health and Passion Sense rolls on page 348, which I presume are part of the system for Life/Death-sight, but cannot find these rolls mentioned anywhere else in the book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23866-thedisreputablemog","name":"TheDisreputableMog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T14:19:10-08:00","id":1184890,"title":"","content":"Pg 234. The second to last sentence of Devil's Dare has a random paragraph break at the word Angst, even though it's the middle of a sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T14:35:55-08:00","id":1184898,"title":"","content":"Page 235 &quot;Botching a roll when the Shadow is dominant: Shadows hate failure. A botch on any roll made by a Shadow-dominated character results in the loss of one point of temporary Angst per one rolled above the number of successes.&quot;<br /> <br /> The reference to over the number of successes is invoking 2nd edition botch rules. If there were any successes in the role it is not a botch according to current botch rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T14:53:08-08:00","id":1184902,"title":"","content":"p61 &quot;A Necropolis is the standard term for a Hierarchy outpost in the <b>Shadowlands. usuall</b>y overlaying some mortal city or other.&quot; Sentences should be joined with a comma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T17:24:01-08:00","id":1184962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184157-wraith20-backer-errata-thread?p=1184420#post1184420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s vestigial Dodge in the Talents writeup and on the character-sheet, despite actual action mechanics using Athletics for dodging as in the other 20th Anniversary games.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSimilarly, Leadership is listed as a Skill in the text and the Character Sheet, but in the other 20th Anniversary editions, Leadership is now a Talent. (Leadership was a Skill in Wraith 1st and 2nd.) Perhaps if/when you remove Dodge from the Talent list, replace it with Leadership. That leaves you room for one more Skill -- perhaps Survival as in the other 20th Anniversary editions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23865-wichtln","name":"wichtln","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T17:40:20-08:00","id":1184966,"title":"","content":"p. 31 &quot;They might be lost to the living, but the dead would never feel their lack&quot;<br /> <br /> Incomplete sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T18:59:37-08:00","id":1184978,"title":"","content":"p65: &quot;But not every wraith is willing to align with <b>it, Those</b> whose disagreements with Stygia are political are loosely grouped under the umbrella of Renegades, while those whose opinion is more religious or spiritual are often referred to as Heretics.&quot; Comma splice error.<br /> <br /> p66: &quot;Some are cults <b>are </b>personality, while others are purely democratic, and still others use trial by combat, feats of strength and anything else imaginable to determine whose word is law.&quot; Are = of<br /> <br /> p67: &quot;Those who had once been Fishers, leading the questing Restless across the Sea of <b>Shadows became</b> outlawed, functionally the first Heretics.&quot; A comma between S<i>hadows</i> and <i>became</i> would improve readability.<br /> <br /> p68: &quot;Students of Stygian history are aware <b>the</b> Charon himself was once a Ferryman, and that the so-called Oath-Circle of the Oar predates Stygia itself.&quot; the = that<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","user":"Callishka","date":". 02-12-2018, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T19:59:06-08:00","id":1184995,"title":"","content":"The writeup of Inner Peace, p. 462 seems confusing and imperfectly transferred from the Dark Kingdom of Jade version. W20 writeup says &quot;If the wraith wins, the two may act together, allowing the wraith to gain Pathos from Passions, Dark Passions, and the use of the p\u2019o\u2019s Thorns. (...). The joining of the two aspects ends when the wraith exhausts all of the p\u2019o\u2019s temporary Angst, or 24 hours have passed&quot;. There are two problems here: first, there seems to be no clear way for the joined wraith to consume temporary Angst according to this writeup (perhaps by using it as Pathos? If so, it should be explictly told), and second it is hard to tell which Thorns might conceivably grant Pathos to the joined wraith (maybe Infamy and/or Vampiric Nature, but hardly everything else).<br /> <br /> In comparison, the original DKoJ version seems much easier to understand and use &quot;The player gets Pathos from both his Dark Passions and his hun's Passions, and may use both his own Arcanos and the p'o's Thorns, drawing upon both his temporary Angst and his Pathos.&quot; As a rule, it is much easier to see how and why a joined wraith may use Thorns to his own advantage (e.g. Tainted Relic, Shadow Traits, Shadowed Face, Shadowplay, Shadow Familiar), and this may even incorporate use of Infamy or Vampiric Nature to gain Pathos. Moreover, the original version explictly tells the joined wraith may use temporary Angst as Pathos, and so consume it. A rewrite of the power according to the original DKoJ version to clarify its use and purpose seems in order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 02-12-2018, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custo