ps://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T08:16:43-08:00","id":1185192,"title":"","content":"Has the Resources Background been definitely removed? The book mentions in several passages the question of the economy among the dead, the currency etc, that is the reason of my observation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23868-fspardoner","name":"fspardoner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23868_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T08:54:08-08:00","id":1185207,"title":"","content":"Missread...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23863,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23863-gothmate","user":"gothmate","date":". 02-19-2018, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23863-gothmate","name":"gothmate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T09:10:17-08:00","id":1185218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gothmate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184157-wraith20-backer-errata-thread?p=1185207#post1185207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p.27 Setting History of the Dark Kingdom of Iron - &amp;quot;not every detail is portrayed or examined to the nth (missing letter?) degree&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's likely accurate, as it's a common saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Nth_Degree\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Nth_Degree\" target=\"_blank\"> The Nth Degree - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Nth_Degree\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Nth_Degree </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T10:18:13-08:00","id":1185244,"title":"","content":"Page 149. &quot;ARCANOS OPTIMIZATION. The dice pool for each art is Attribute + Arcanos. All Arcanoi use only two attributes. In most cases, these are attributes from the same category: either Physical, Social, or Mental.&quot;<br /> <br /> But Castigate uses Perception (Soulsight), Charisma (Playing With Fire), Stamina (Bulwalk), and Intelligence (Trimming The Black Rose). <br /> <br /> I am still reading Castigate, but it is good to check this question in all Arcanoi, if it is really a misunderstanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23868-fspardoner","name":"fspardoner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23868_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T10:41:29-08:00","id":1185260,"title":"","content":"The Haunters are in the wrong spot in the Guild list. Pandamonium comes before Phantasm, not after Puppeteering. So, Haunters should come after Spooks and before Sandmen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T10:47:01-08:00","id":1185266,"title":"","content":"Embody - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Harrow the Mortal Flesh (Initiate)<br /> <br /> &quot;If the target dies or is Soulforged while in the Shadowlands, the Proctor\u2019s Shadow gains 10 temporary Angst. If she dies, she automatically becomes a Spectre.&quot;<br /> <br /> A hint for truism:<br /> <br /> &quot;If the target dies or is Soulforged while in the Shadowlands, the Proctor\u2019s Shadow gains 10 temporary Angst. If she dies, she automatically becomes a Spectre <b>too</b>.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23868-fspardoner","name":"fspardoner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23868_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T10:59:53-08:00","id":1185271,"title":"","content":"p70: &quot;The citizens of Stygia, its Necropoli, and its outposts spend most of their time sifting through the chaos of being the receptacle of untold numbers of souls every <b>deal</b>.&quot; The word <i>deal</i> seems odd. Should that be <i>day</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T11:13:40-08:00","id":1185278,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this qualifies as errata or not, but it's a small detail so ...<br /> <br /> In Artifact Aircrafts on p. 317 the Wright Flyer and &quot;Glamorous Glennis&quot; are listed. Neither of these real historical aircraft were destroyed. In fact they're both on display at the Smithsonian Institution's Air and Space Museum in Washington D.C.!<br /> <br /> For the Wright Flyer, I would suggest using the Wright Military Flyer (also known as the Wright Model A) . This aircraft crashed during a demonstration flight in 1908 that led to the first modern aircraft fatality. Relic material for sure! <br /> <br /> &quot;Glamorous Glennis&quot; is more difficult to substitute. Some X-planes were destroyed after Yeager's flight but few were as noteworthy. The X-2 in particular was lost during a record-breaking flight. Or perhaps a De Havilland Comet which was the first operating jet airliner, several of which were lost due to structural failures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4459-levity-gallows","name":"Levity Gallows","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T13:09:33-08:00","id":1185318,"title":"","content":"Pg. 409 Humans in the Underworld sidebar has either superfluous text or an incomplete additional sentence involving other Awakened.<br /> &quot;As the Benandanti cross in spirit form, their auras are subtler, and the dif-ficulty is raised to 8.Other Awakened &quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T14:10:16-08:00","id":1185343,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Nevermind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 02-12-2018, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T14:43:01-08:00","id":1185355,"title":"","content":"p.34 The Hierarchy - Eqitaes (typing error) on the last paragraph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23863-gothmate","name":"gothmate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T16:13:33-08:00","id":1185384,"title":"","content":"Multiple pages: The river that ends at the Sea of Souls is called the River of Death a few times... until the sidebar on page 76, where it starts being called Styx or the River Styx. Obviously, these are the same rivers, but a new player, or one unfamiliar with Greek mythos, may not understand the name change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T16:39:26-08:00","id":1185395,"title":"","content":"p. 162 (p. 227 of the pdf), &quot;Charon sought counsel from Grand High Oracle Serena&quot; - should be Selena","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","name":"Asimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T16:41:56-08:00","id":1185397,"title":"","content":"It does appear it needs to be clarified what happens when you spend a point of corpus for an arcanos - presumably its bashing damage, but this needs to be specified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T16:51:43-08:00","id":1185404,"title":"","content":"p80 &quot;Many cutting-edge ideas come from the Salon, particularly among the scientific contingent, said to be working on cures for cancer and other diseases in order to bring more wraiths into the <b>Grim Legion</b>\u2019s purview.&quot; Should be Iron Legion, not Grim Legion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T18:43:57-08:00","id":1185440,"title":"","content":"On the page 236 says &quot;In order for the Shadow to take control of a character, the Shadow and the Psyche face off against one another. The Shadow spends a point of temporary Angst and rolls on her adjusted temporary Angst rating. The Psyche may resist by rolling her permanent Willpower, plus any Eidolon dice she may possess (see \u201cEidolon,\u201d p. 143).&quot;<br /> <br /> And on the page 230 says &quot;When a wraith\u2019s temporary Angst exceeds her Willpower, the Shadow can attempt to usurp control of the Corpus by means of a Catharsis roll (see p. 236)&quot;<br /> <br /> For the sake of clarity, is there a need for the temporary Angst level to be greater than the psyche's permanent Willpower to enable the Catharsis roll? If the wraith has Willpower 10, the character will it be immune to Catharsis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23868-fspardoner","name":"fspardoner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23868_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T19:29:45-08:00","id":1185456,"title":"","content":"pg. 44: &quot;The two main classes of items in the Underworld are relics and Artifacts. relics come from the Skinlands.&quot; Change period to comma.<br /> <br /> pg. 47: &quot;the chains weree long since repurposed&quot; Change &quot;weree&quot; to &quot;were.&quot;<br /> <br /> pg. 47: &quot;In a few instances. coffles of thralls have worked together&quot; Change period to comma.<br /> <br /> pg. 50: &quot;It is the capital of Charon\u2019s venerable empire and it is the place to see and be seen among the dead.&quot; Insert comma between &quot;empire&quot; and &quot;and.&quot;<br /> <br /> pg. 51: &quot;Students of history will constantly find marvels here, that is, if they\u2019re not run over by foot traffic while they gawk.&quot; Change the first comma to a period or a semi-colon.<br /> <br /> pg. 61: &quot;A Necropolis is the standard term for a Hierarchy outpost in the Shadowlands. usually overlaying some mortal city or other.&quot; Change period to comma.<br /> <br /> pg. 63: &quot;the days of the Paris Commune having set up an alternative Necropolis&quot; Insert comma between &quot;Commune&quot; and &quot;having.&quot; Change &quot;having&quot; to &quot;have.&quot;<br /> <br /> pg. 66: &quot;Some are cults are personality&quot; Change second &quot;are&quot; to &quot;of.&quot;<br /> <br /> pg. 67: &quot;Those who had once been Fishers, leading the questing Restless across the Sea of Shadows became outlawed&quot; Insert comma between &quot;Shadows&quot; and &quot;became.&quot;<br /> <br /> pg. 71: &quot;even if the long-term consequences not&quot; Insert &quot;are&quot; between &quot;consequences&quot; and &quot;not.&quot;<br /> <br /> pg. 153: Bold &quot;System:&quot;<br /> <br /> pg. 227-228: Is the Grand High Oracle Serena or Selena? Both are used.<br /> <br /> pg. 170: Bold &quot;System:&quot; under Render Relic.<br /> <br /> pg. 374: Delete tab before &quot;modifications below.&quot;<br /> <br /> pg. 425: &quot;mother-of-pearl inlay in the oak handle. appears fairly innocuous.&quot; Change period to comma.<br /> <br /> pg. 435: &quot;Regardless of the family\u2019s focus, wraiths still address each other using familial terms (e.g. aunt, older brother, younger cousin, grandmother.)&quot; Put closing period after parenthesis.<br /> <br /> pg. 440: &quot;Many skilled wraiths with talents in Arcanoi usually only found in the Jade kingdom&quot; Capitalize &quot;kingdom.&quot;<br /> <br /> pg. 457: &quot;Others of Les Imvisibles make the journey&quot; Change &quot;Imvisibles&quot; to &quot;Invisibles.&quot;<br /> <br /> pg. 457: &quot;Les lnvisibles: The term Creole wraiths use to describe themselves.&quot; Hard to see due to the font, but the capital &quot;eye&quot; in &quot;Invisibles&quot; is actually a lowercase &quot;ell.&quot; Change to capital &quot;eye.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T22:04:53-08:00","id":1185491,"title":"","content":"I feel like there is quite a bit missing from Chapter 2. Starting at page 25 we begin a discussion of the geography of the underworld: The Skinlands, The Shroud and the Fog, The Underworld (in broadest terms) and where I would expect the text to start talking about specific things in the underworld like The Shadowlands, The Tempest, The Sunless Sea, The Far Shores, etc. Instead, it starts talking about Oblivion, and then the History of the Underworld. Almost like it skipped to the middle of the proverbial onion.<br /> <br /> I have looked elsewhere for the section detailing these locations and I cannot find it anywhere... which makes me think that this section was omitted by mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","user":"Froggy711","date":". 02-13-2018, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T01:34:21-08:00","id":1185517,"title":"","content":"p91: &quot;The <b>once</b> exception to Stygia\u2019s laissez-faire approach on Guilds is the case of the so-called Forbidden Guilds.&quot; once = one<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T08:40:41-08:00","id":1185594,"title":"","content":"p19: Really confusing Underworld geography. So: &quot;Howling beneath the placid surface of the waters is the Tempest, the eternal storm...&quot; What waters? The only body of water mentioned in that section is the Sunless Sea: &quot;Sitting across the Underworld from Stygia, the Far Shores are an endless archipelago of islands in the Sunless Sea.&quot; Those can't be the waters in question because that would imply that Stygia and the Far Shores are above the Tempest, and Stygia clearly isn't. From the same section: &quot;Rare islands if stability exist within the endless winds; Stygia is built on one, and other Dark Kingdoms are known to stand against the storm as well.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> p26: &quot;Children and animals <b>in particular</b> are immune to its effects... Cats <b>in particular</b> are known for watching wraiths...&quot;<br /> <br /> Also p26: The first line of the section The Shroud and the Fog: &quot;The realms of the dead are collectively known as the Underworld...&quot; The first line of the very next section: &quot;The Underworld is the collective term for all the realms of the dead.&quot; It's redundant to say the same thing twice on the same page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T09:42:55-08:00","id":1185615,"title":"","content":"deleted. I misread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","user":"Callishka","date":". 02-13-2018, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T12:13:24-08:00","id":1185684,"title":"","content":"I legitimately can't tell if this is a mistake or intentional.<br /> <br /> p35: The Great Evacuation. Charon exiled all the Shining Ones from Stygia before he ever found out they were corrupt. It might be that this section was supposed to refer to the Fishers and not the Shining Ones. It might be that this section was supposed to come after he found out what was going on in the Far Shores. Or it might be that this was intentional and Charon was taking out his anger at the Fishers on all those from the Far Shores. Not sure which so I'm flagging it.<br /> <br /> Also, point of clarification, errata wise does it matter if a sidebar appears a page early? Like how the Doomslayer sidebar appears on pg 39 and Doomslayers aren't mentioned until pg 40?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T14:40:52-08:00","id":1185727,"title":"","content":"[page 148] For any common art, Guild instruction takes one consecutive day per dot of the art\u2019s rating, and the art\u2019s experience point cost is reduced to current rating x2 experience (or a flat 5 experience for a new Arcanos). See p. 301 for the character-development rules.<br /> <br /> [page 303] Having a Mentor versed in the relevant Arcanos is useful, however, as is a membership in the appropriate Guild. If conditions permit, the player may roll the relevant Background rating when trying to learn a new Arcanos (difficulty 6). Each success reduces the experience-point cost of the Arcanos by one, to a minimum of one.<br /> <br /> Is it a divergence in the rules or is it just my impression?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23868-fspardoner","name":"fspardoner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23868_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T21:53:44-08:00","id":1185830,"title":"","content":"p161 &quot;If the target was willing, she loses 1 temporary Willpower and the Proctor\u2019s <b>Shadow gains 1 Angst</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm going to assume this was supposed to be &quot;temporary angst&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13276-bristark","name":"Bristark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13276_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T06:09:07-08:00","id":1185915,"title":"","content":"This isn't really an erratum, but...the arcanoi each have the guild name, but are sorted by arcanos name, and there's no place that really prominently lists the arcanos name at any kind of header level. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12711-prester-jane","name":"Prester Jane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T12:45:54-08:00","id":1186043,"title":"","content":"p.44 - Relics and Artifacts: &quot;Anything that comes out of the forges is a considered an Artifact&quot; (correct is &quot;is considered an Artifact&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23863-gothmate","name":"gothmate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T14:44:57-08:00","id":1186079,"title":"","content":"p.49 - Catharsis and Harrowing - Far worse than a bout of Catharsis is a Harrowing. (a bout is splited)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23863-gothmate","name":"gothmate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T20:06:31-08:00","id":1186165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gothmate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184157-wraith20-backer-errata-thread?p=1186079#post1186079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p.49 - Catharsis and Harrowing - Far worse than a bout of Catharsis is a Harrowing. (a bout is splited)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bout\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/static/images/icons/enwiktionary.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bout\" target=\"_blank\"> bout - Wiktionary, the free dictionary </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bout\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bout </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1. A period of something, usually painful or unpleasant. <i>A <b>bout</b> of drought</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T01:23:52-08:00","id":1186209,"title":"","content":"P. 68 \u201cAll of these horrors are woven into the fabric the Hierarchy...\u201d <br /> <br /> Insert \u201cof\u201d in between \u201cfabric\u201d and \u201cthe\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T08:05:43-08:00","id":1186311,"title":"","content":"P. 103 Thorns and Troupe are listed under Gaming Terms, while all other Wraith specific terms are under Wraith Terms. Demeanor, Nature, and Willpower are under Wraith Terms, while all other terms common to the Storyteller games are under Gaming Terms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23876-karn-dethahal","name":"Karn-Dethahal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T13:36:34-08:00","id":1186393,"title":"","content":"Page 420 of the PDF file:Maleficence 4 Empower: &quot;Spend 1 Angst and 1 Willpower to trigger this art, plus 5 additional Angst points for each dot of the Dark Arcanos power you wish to bestow (bestowing a basic ability costs 3 Angst points).&quot;<br /> <br /> 20th Edition removed basic abilities from Arcanoi. Recommend deleting everything in parenthesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T13:45:09-08:00","id":1186397,"title":"","content":"Page lviii: there's a line break in the middle of the word &quot;the&quot;: <br /> This is the Kiss of Death. You see<br /> now who I am. I am t<br /> he incarnation of Death<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23887-gjallerbru","name":"gjallerbru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T14:20:50-08:00","id":1186414,"title":"","content":"Page 420 of the PDF file:Maleficence 5 Conversion: The entire write up is confusing in regards to Spectres. Under the 20th edition rules, Spectres have a Willpower score and a permanent Pathos score that represents the strength of the Psyche. Conversion as describes allows for the lowering of Willpower or the raising of Permanent Angst. It calls out Spectres in the description. Spectres already have a permanent Angst of 10. As written this power can only lower Spectres Willpower. Reading the description, it seems as if it should be able to permanently lower Specte Pathos rating.<br /> <br /> This is more of a clarification suggestion. If the intent of Conversion is to affect Wraiths, or lower the Willpower of Spectres, then slight wording would simplify this. If the intent of Conversion is to also be able to lower the permanent Pathos rating of a spectre's Psyche, this to needs to be clarified.<br /> <br /> The intent of the art on Wraiths is obvious, create Drones or Spectres. WIth Spectre's; can this ability weaken a Spectre's better half, or is it just meant to make them have less Willpower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T00:02:49-08:00","id":1186562,"title":"","content":"Pg 171 The Relicforging side at states that characters with Status (Artificers Guild) 3 or higher may know the relicforging process if their knowledge of Flux is high enough. I think that is meant to be Status (<b>Alchemist</b> Guild)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T10:59:17-08:00","id":1186733,"title":"","content":"p56-57 &quot;The Seat of Shadows, home of the Iron Legion and its Ashen Lady, rests on the northernmost of the \u201cseven hills\u201d along the Road of Lords, and it sets the tone for the whole district. <b>Each morning</b> it appears in the <b>dawn light</b> as a beautiful, darkly gleaming grove of soulsteel and Veinous Stair stone spires, rising almost as high as Charon\u2019s own Onyx Tower. As the <b>day passes</b>, it seems to age and crumble, and at <b>night </b>it\u2019s a tangle of ruins punctuated by only a few usable halls and chambers. Then <b>dawn</b> comes and it renews again. Many buildings in Ironville do the same, out of a shared emotional resonance.&quot;<br /> <br /> There is dawn light and evening darkness in Stygia? In what sense is the Sunless Sea sunless, then?<br /> <br /> p154 &quot;Hung outside a building, the lantern advertises a Pardoner\u2019s services; carried by <b>her </b>it illuminates <b>his </b>way in the darkest of places. Each lantern\u2019s unique to the Pardoner who owns it, for <b>she </b>either creates it herself as part of <b>his</b> \u201capprenticeship\u201d (or, more rarely, gets it from a master who knows <b>him </b>well), <b>but most Pardoners</b> favor traditional designs with baroque, macabre adornments.&quot;<br /> <br /> The pronouns are switching within the same phrase, yet refer to the same individual. Highly confusing. In addition, the use of a parenthetical phrase clashes with the &quot;either&quot;. You can't use &quot;either&quot; to contrast a pair of items in a sentence, and then put the second item inside parentheses, or else the reader will look for the second item <i>after</i> the end of the parenthetical. If it's important enough to be connected to the &quot;either&quot;, it should stand on its own and not be slipped into a parenthetical aside. Finally, the &quot;but most Pardoners...&quot; clause should probably be in its own sentence. This whole passage could use a rewrite to be comprehended on a first reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","user":"Callishka","date":". 02-16-2018, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T11:19:19-08:00","id":1186745,"title":"","content":"This was addressed in another thread, but so far no one has posted here as an errata, and I suppose this needs at least a second look at: p. 56-57, Ironville section, speaks of &quot;dawn light&quot; illuminating the Seat of Shadows each morning.<br /> <br /> It really seems a poetical liberty that goes radically counter the established setting. There is no sunlight (or even natural occurring light) in Stygia, the Tempest, or bellow/beyond. Stygia itself counts hours by sea tides and water clocks. The closest there is to natural illumination is light from the Shadowlands coming from Nihils appearing as stars on the sky.<br /> <br /> It would be better to remove the reference to light and state that the Seat of Shadows simply seems to grow older with each cycle os Stygian time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":412,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","user":"valismedsen","date":".  ops, Callishka beat me to it. sorry 02-16-2018, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T17:15:28-08:00","id":1186873,"title":"","content":"[page 152] &quot;System: The wraith ignores the difficulty penalties that normally apply outside the Shadowlands while she has unresolved Fetters. This art is always active, requires no roll, and can\u2019t be shared.&quot;<br /> <br /> Would be nice make a page reference of these difficulty penalties. There are page references for much less.<br /> <br /> <br /> [page 316] &quot;Your character may spend an amount of Pathos equal to his per-turn rating.&quot; <br /> <br /> Where's its information?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23868-fspardoner","name":"fspardoner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23868_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T17:42:41-08:00","id":1186880,"title":"","content":"[page 348] &quot;Additionally, a Spectre\u2019s focus is always on the negative, with the goal of twisting the [period break]<br /> information gleaned to their own dark ends. This is managed largely through roleplay and description, but can be essential to convey the warped outlook that Spectres have.&quot;<br /> <br /> [page 355 and 173] Level 5 of Maleficence and Inhabit have the same name. All right?<br /> <br /> [page 457] &quot;Under very rare circumstances, if not specifically stated otherwise, Stygian wraiths may be able to learn some of the Arcanoi of other Dark Kingdoms. Doing so [?]&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bApparently, the text was terminated suddenly, without conclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23868-fspardoner","user":"fspardoner","date":". 02-16-2018, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23868-fspardoner","name":"fspardoner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23868_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T20:59:28-08:00","id":1186926,"title":"","content":"<b>[169]:</b> The box &quot;A Bottle in Front of Me&quot; seems to refer to the Usury Arcanos, but it's in the section on Flux.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, it looks like there's a power on the next page that this actually refers to, but the box is confusing because you'll have to turn the page to see the context that makes it make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":215,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","user":"Rand Brittain","date":". 02-17-2018, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T11:42:58-08:00","id":1187095,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 35: </b>&quot;Taking as their model the Catholic <b>church</b>\u2019s Inquisition in Europe...&quot; -- church should be capitalized<br /> <br /> <b>p. 170: </b>&quot;<i>System: </i>The Alchemist spends five minutes in concentration...&quot; -- the word System should be bold<br /> <br /> <b>p. 183, Cacophony system: </b>&quot;The player rolls <b>Willpower </b>+ Keening.&quot; -- Unless there are meant to be exceptions beyond the forbidden Arcanoi, this goes against the wording of the <i>Arcanos Optimization </i>sidebar on p. 149 (i.e., this should be rolled with Charisma or Manipulation). Also, none of the other Arcanoi use Willpower in the activation roll<br /> <br /> <b>p. 184, Crescendo system: </b>&quot;The player rolls <b>Stamina </b>+ Keening...&quot; -- As above, this should be Charisma/Manipulation<br /> <br /> <b>p. 184, Out of Tune system: </b>&quot;The player rolls <b>Intelligence </b>+ Keening...&quot; -- As above, this should be Charisma/Manipulation<br /> <br /> <b>pp. 196-198, Moliate mechanics: </b>As above, but the systems for Moliate don't use a consistent pair of Attributes at all (Dex, Int, Manip, Perception, Stamina, Strength, and Wits are all used, with Dex being the more common one)<br /> <br /> <b>p. 200, Stonehand Punch: </b>&quot;<i>System: </i>The player spends 1 Pathos and makes a normal Brawl attack.&quot; -- System should be bold<br /> <br /> <b>pp. 209-211, Phantasm mechanics: </b>As with Moliate, there's no consistent pair of Attributes for activation rolls<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b><br /> <br /> <b>pp. 155-157, Castigate mechanics:</b> As with Moliate/Phantasm, there's no consistent pair of Attributes for activation rolls (Charisma is the most common)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 02-17-2018, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T17:09:36-08:00","id":1187172,"title":"","content":"p 200 Stonehand Punch: The text does not specify what type of damage the Arcanos technique inflicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T02:46:20-08:00","id":1187254,"title":"","content":"P. 146 lists the Alchemists and Artificers as allies, but this is overtly contradicted by pages 167 and 168, which describe the Artifercers as the main force behind hostility toward the Alchemists and areas WITHOUT strong Artificer influence being where Alchemists are able to freely operate.<br /> <br /> Edit: on reread I see the &quot;allied&quot; moniker may be a misnomer to mechanically represent their connected history that gives them access to shared Arcanoi lore, so this may be a non-issue. The idea that the &quot;Allied&quot; guilds aren't necessarily allies at all could have been made clearer though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-18-2018, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T13:28:15-08:00","id":1187343,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 481: </b>The Poltergeist Shade has Castigate as a favored Arcanos, but p. 478 notes that most Castigate powers fail for Projector characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T00:44:37-08:00","id":1187484,"title":"","content":"The Displace write up on pages 463 and 464 refer to another Arcanos named &quot;Kinesis&quot;. The word doesn't appear anywhere else in the book.<br /> <br /> I think this is a relic of coming from the &quot;Great War&quot; sourcebook. Kinesis was what Inhabit was called in that era. It should probably be changed to Inhabit throughout Displace's writeup.<br /> <br /> Edit: on a similar point, that section refers to the Indian Dark Kingdom as Swar instead of Svarga - another relic of Great War, I assume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-19-2018, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T01:43:32-08:00","id":1187491,"title":"","content":"Gonna add my list so far, so I have at least something up when this thread closes:<br /> <br /> Pg. xli: &quot;The spirit clings to its past, never quite <b>trusting and strong enough to let go</b>.&quot; Really, really weird phrasing here, to the point that I'm not entirely sure what it's trying to say. It's not even poetic or archaic like much of the intro fiction. Just... weird. I guess it could work as needing both of those traits, but it still sounds decidedly &quot;off.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pg. 17: Chapter 10 is listed as being titled &quot;Adversaries,&quot; and containing both Spectres and other creatures of the Underworld. In the book as released, it's simply titled &quot;Spectres&quot; and is solely about Spectres, with other denizens being in Chapter 12.<br /> <br /> Pg. 30: &quot;As their first act, the Senate granted lands to Shining Ones near the docks of the <b>Shining Sea</b>.&quot; There is no mention of a &quot;Shining Sea&quot; elsewhere in the book. It's most likely a mistype of &quot;Sunless Sea.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pg. 49: &quot;<b>They are her</b>, the reasons she feels compelled to continue to defy death.&quot; Now, something definitely went wrong here, but there's a few possibilities. It could be missing a word after &quot;her&quot; that would make this sentence in full read properly. It could be missing emphasis on &quot;are&quot; that makes it clear that it is, in fact, stating that a Wraith <b>is</b> their Passions. It could just be a bit of weird phrasing that sounds off.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fetters are the things she feels most strongly about. They may be things she loved in life: living relatives and loved ones, places where treasured events happened, <b>such as</b> the tools she used in satisfying work.&quot; In this passage, &quot;Such as&quot; should be &quot;or.&quot; Tools are not places, and can't be examples of them, which is what &quot;such as&quot; would mean in this context. Even if that were correct, there'd be a missing &quot;or&quot; before &quot;living.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pg 54, though for context I'm including some text from Pg 51, the error is on 54: &quot;In some places, the less formal and direct roads keep to older, rougher ways; in others, they tunnel <b>over</b> or even pass along the top of the official route.&quot; This should almost definitely be &quot;tunnel under.&quot; There's no mention of anything over the Road of Lords to tunnel through, and even if there were, this would effectively be saying that some paths go above it twice.<br /> <br /> Pg. 54, &quot;An Isle of Legacies&quot; sidebar: &quot;Stygia is a city where the continued memorial interest <b>in</b> the living matters intensely...&quot; This should be <b>of</b> the living, as the full sentence makes it clear it's not about people memorializing the living (which is weird), but about the living's memorial interest in certain buildings.<br /> <br /> Page 69: &quot;It was they who brought Stygia to the table to establish the Covenant of the Millions...&quot; The Covenant of the Millions is mentioned as though it's something readers either should already recognize or will be informed about later -- something of significance that will itself reveal how significant the Ferrymen's role actually is... but it's never mentioned anywhere else in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2836-nezumi","user":"Nezumi","date":". 02-21-2018, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2836-nezumi","name":"Nezumi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T02:13:40-08:00","id":1187495,"title":"","content":"PG 375; In the Background section, it mentions that Spectres may not take the Wealth Background. No such background is detailed in this book.<br /> PG 395; In the second paragraph of the 'Wraith to Risen, Along for the Ride' section, there is another reference to the non-existant Wealth Background.<br /> Pg 463; first sentence mentions a Kinesis Arcanoi. No such Arcanoi is described in the book. Under the Wraithride system description on the same page is a reference to a 'Sense Kinesis' power.<br /> Pg 464; under the Deflect power's system subheading it mentions Kinesis as part of the opposing dice-pool. Again, that power is not in the book<br /> PG 486; Under the 'You Can't Take It With You - Orpheus Backgrounds' heading, there is mention of a Resources Background. Again, not explained in the book.<br /> <br /> Edit: PG 152; Wayffarer's Resolve does not give a page reference for those penalties, nor can they be found in the book. Making the power redundant","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 02-19-2018, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T15:33:27-08:00","id":1187668,"title":"","content":"On Page 355 in the system for Empower the text &quot;(bestowing a basic ability costs 3 Angst points)&quot; appears, but basic abilities are no longer part of the Arcanoi system.<br /> <br /> On Page 377 there is a price listed for Arcanos Basic Ability, but Basic Abilities are no longer part of the Arcanoi system.<br /> <br /> On Page 463 the text &quot;Although Straddle (and the detection of other wraiths using it) is a basic ability for practitioners of this Arcanos, Tvashtriya can have no further interaction with objects across the Shroud.&quot; appears but basic abilities are no longer part of the system.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T15:57:30-08:00","id":1187671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184157-wraith20-backer-errata-thread?p=1187495#post1187495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: PG 152; Wayffarer's Resolve does not give a page reference for those penalties, nor can they be found in the book. Making the power redundant</div> </div> </div> </div>Expanding on this - if there are intended to be penalties exploring and acting in the lower Underworld for Wraiths with remaining Fetters, those rules need to be added in the book somewhere that makes sense (like the mechanical effects of Fetters), because they currently don't seem to exist or can't be found.<br /> <br /> If they AREN'T supposed to be a problem, then Wayfarer's Resolve needs to be completely replaced, as it doesn't do anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T16:02:06-08:00","id":1187673,"title":"","content":"Page 235 has the text &quot;For example, a wraith who uses Castigate \u2022 (Coax) to acquire additional dice from her Shadow&quot;, but Coax is not a power in Way of the Soul, not Castigate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T16:03:36-08:00","id":1187674,"title":"","content":"Page 461 has the text &quot;System: To use Coax, rollWay of the Soul against&quot;. There should be a space between roll and Way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T18:19:19-08:00","id":1187707,"title":"","content":"p.162: &quot;which lends Oracles an oft-warranted reputation for vagueness and evasion. (oft-warranted &gt;&gt; missed letter?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23863-gothmate","name":"gothmate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T00:33:25-08:00","id":1187768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gothmate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184157-wraith20-backer-errata-thread?p=1187707#post1187707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p.162: &quot;which lends Oracles an oft-warranted reputation for vagueness and evasion. (oft-warranted &gt;&gt; missed letter?)</div> </div> </div> </div>The meaning of &quot;oft-warranted&quot; is &quot;often well-deserved&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13535-leftmost-cat","name":"Leftmost Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T00:53:27-08:00","id":1187772,"title":"","content":"p.71 &quot;An Anacreon\u2019s <i><b>overlords</b></i> may be considered equal to colonels and, when an Anacreon has more than one <i><b>overlord</b></i>, they make up his command staff.&quot;<br /> <br /> Should be capitalized to &quot;Overlords&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T12:40:42-08:00","id":1187940,"title":"","content":"PG 302 Trait Cost table references Merits but not Flaws. Additionally, there isn't a Merits and Flaw section in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23909-sanguinist18","name":"sanguinist18","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T18:04:34-08:00","id":1188040,"title":"","content":"p498: <b>Wraith backers</b><br /> <br /> 'Jesika Wolff' should be '<b>Alyx Wulf</b>'<br /> <br /> (Please msg me if you need to verify this change. Thanks!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23893-alyxwulf","name":"alyxwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T19:25:31-08:00","id":1188057,"title":"","content":"Seems like the entire merits/flaws section got left on the cutting room floor. Can we get that remedied before actual launch or is it planned to leave unfinished?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23916-tahllon","name":"Tahllon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T05:29:51-08:00","id":1188143,"title":"","content":"Page 89 &quot;They used the Skinlands for both covert channels of communication and the distribution of <b>materiel</b>.&quot; Should be &quot;material.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T08:34:26-08:00","id":1188179,"title":"","content":"Not a grammar or spelling thing but...<br /> <br /> In the old Wraith one of the consequences of the Third Great Maelstrom was the Tempest. Prior to the Third Maelstrom the Sea of Shadows was far more placid. I haven't finished reading thru the book yet so maybe this is addressed later but cosmologically it seems enormous to remove this from the setting. Is this stated later on? If not, can we put a sentence in there along with the thickening of the Shroud that this was when the Tempest came about?<br /> <br /> JSun<br /> <br /> (1 week later....)<br /> Oh. Okay. It's on page 447. Well that's tucked away. I think I'd still prefer it in the main timeline but hey, at least it's here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12023,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","user":"MMSPR","date":". 03-06-2018, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T11:20:41-08:00","id":1188241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184157-wraith20-backer-errata-thread?p=1188143#post1188143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 89 &quot;They used the Skinlands for both covert channels of communication and the distribution of <b>materiel</b>.&quot; Should be &quot;material.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a real word: it means arms and ammunition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T11:33:43-08:00","id":1188245,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. With communication in the sentence, I thought there were referring to propaganda or information. Moving arms and ammunition through the Skinlands is do-able, I guess. Move them some place and then destroy them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T19:14:26-08:00","id":1188370,"title":"","content":"Bottom of page 55, right hand column, says that Riverside District is on the western shore. The map's not done yet, I get it, but the geography described leads me to think this should say the eastern shore, and the following paragraph on page 56 seems to substantiate this I think. <br /> <br /> JSun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T20:13:08-08:00","id":1189095,"title":"","content":"Page 88 talks about the War of the Guilds being a result of the First Maelstrom, which is dated as starting in 476 AD. Yet the date for the War of the Guilds is listed as 1358 AD. The prelude to the War of the Guilds was 900 years and started only 11 years after the founding of the Guilds in 1347, and after the Second Maelstrom? The general timeline on page 34 and the Guild timeline on page 88 seem out of whack, or maybe need further clarifying. Or perhaps on page 88 that's a reference to the Second Great Maelstrom instead of the first?<br /> <br /> -JSun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T22:42:28-08:00","id":1189350,"title":"","content":"Reread Displace and even more frustrating copy pasta on top of the &quot;Kinesis&quot; and &quot;Swar&quot; issues.<br /> <br /> &quot;Glow&quot; a Moliate art that doesn't exist in Wraith20 is referenced, and the general tvashtriya text is written in the historic context of the British bringing Colonial Indian forces to Western battlefields.<br /> <br /> I haven't done a one to one comparison, but if someone was paid for rewriting and updating Displace, Onyx Path was conned. They copied out of Wraith:the Great War rather than writing the word count they were paid for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T06:29:29-08:00","id":1189391,"title":"","content":"P. 360 (425 of the pdf), there is no transition between the end of the Shadecraft section, who ends the Dark Arcanoi section, and the Mortwights description, who begins the Specter's caste description. A Title and a introduction of the section seems missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","name":"Asimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T01:31:14-08:00","id":1189554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184157-wraith20-backer-errata-thread?p=1189350#post1189350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reread Displace and even more frustrating copy pasta on top of the &quot;Kinesis&quot; and &quot;Swar&quot; issues.<br /> <br /> &quot;Glow&quot; a Moliate art that doesn't exist in Wraith20 is referenced, and the general tvashtriya text is written in the historic context of the British bringing Colonial Indian forces to Western battlefields.<br /> <br /> I haven't done a one to one comparison, but if someone was paid for rewriting and updating Displace, Onyx Path was conned. They copied out of Wraith:the Great War rather than writing the word count they were paid for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not to keep beating this drum, but Behest also appears to be simply copypasted out of Great War rather than actually written for this book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T14:07:14-08:00","id":1189686,"title":"","content":"p. 108 &quot;During character creation, feel free set limits if you feel you need them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Insert &quot;to&quot; in between &quot;free&quot; and &quot;set&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T21:09:51-08:00","id":1189765,"title":"","content":"Page 115 says that when you spend a point of Willpower you get a standard success, as opposed to rolling 10.<br /> \ud83e\udd14<br /> Nowhere in the rules that I have read does rolling a 10 do anything special. Does it &quot;explode&quot; and let you reroll? Does it count as 2 successes? We know what rolling a 1 does. 10's aren't mentioned. <br /> <br /> -JSun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T21:11:58-08:00","id":1189766,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it was mentioned yet but, the Arcanoi for Carribean Wraiths was mentioned but, not included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13097-mrblack83","name":"MrBlack83","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T05:13:40-08:00","id":1189832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MMSPR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184157-wraith20-backer-errata-thread?p=1189765#post1189765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 115 says that when you spend a point of Willpower you get a standard success, as opposed to rolling 10.<br /> \ud83e\udd14<br /> Nowhere in the rules that I have read does rolling a 10 do anything special. Does it &quot;explode&quot; and let you reroll? Does it count as 2 successes? We know what rolling a 1 does. 10's aren't mentioned.<br /> <br /> -JSun</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Page 125 under Specialties has the information you're looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T06:50:0