&quot;dump stat&quot;. But I could totally see making it a useful stat for Embody and Moliate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T17:29:53-08:00","id":1190860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MMSPR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184157-wraith20-backer-errata-thread?p=1190834#post1190834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't it be neat if you rolled Appearance for some of the Embody and Moliate Arts (like Statue)? I don't know any Storyteller that gets a whole lot of use out of that attribute. It's the &amp;quot;dump stat&amp;quot;. But I could totally see making it a useful stat for Embody and Moliate.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to discuss something, please start a new thread, as this thread is for errata for Wraith20. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T18:24:37-08:00","id":1190869,"title":"","content":"On page 168 top of the right-hand column, for Flux it says &quot;As with a normal feat of strength, the player may roll Willpower (difficulty 6) to increase the Wraith's effective Flux.&quot; <br /> <br /> Normally that would be difficulty 9 (as stated on page 320). I can't tell if this is supposed to be a Willpower roll at Difficulty 9 (like a Feat of Strength) or if this is maybe like a feat of strength (&quot;but at difficulty 6&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T20:03:33-08:00","id":1190892,"title":"","content":"Continuing with the &quot;All Arcanoi use only two attributes&quot; thread...<br /> <br /> Most of the Keening Arts are Charisma and Manipulation, but one is Stamina, one is Intelligence, and most curiously one is Willpower+Keening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T23:23:30-08:00","id":1190912,"title":"","content":"p 161 &quot;If the target dies or is Soulforged while in the Shadowlands, the Proctor\u2019s Shadow gains 10 temporary Angst. <b>If she dies, she automatically becomes a Spectre.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> Unclear language.<br /> <br /> Unsure if the sentence is suggesting that the Proctor wraith becomes a Spectre if they die, or if that the Proctor becomes a Spectre in addition to gaining 10 temporary Angst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T06:18:12-08:00","id":1190957,"title":"","content":"Under Moliate's Sculpt...<br /> &quot;He cannot, however, create additional or alternate sensory organs.&quot;<br /> ...<br /> &quot;Additional sensory organs created by Moliate are fully functional...&quot;<br /> <br /> These two sentences under the same art seem to contradict each other and raise the question whether or not Sculpt lets you create additional sensory organs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T07:25:18-08:00","id":1190972,"title":"","content":"Under Moliate 4's &quot;Rend&quot;, touching a target is said to use Dexterity + Melee. In most White Wolf games that would be Dex+Brawl. I guess I can see, if you've used Armory, that you would use Melee in that case, but I think Brawl would generally be more appropriate (like with Vicissitude). I'm assuming Rend can't be used with a baseball bat.<br /> <br /> (Same with the level 5 power &quot;Savage&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12023,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","user":"MMSPR","date":". 03-02-2018, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T07:35:12-08:00","id":1190975,"title":"","content":"Continuing with the &quot;all Arcanoi use only two attributes&quot; thread...<br /> <br /> Moliate uses Dexterity, Perception, Manipulation, Intelligence, Stamina, Strength, and Wits. <br /> <br /> Ironically, the Aracanos that most affects appearance uses most everything but Appearance. \ud83d\ude01","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T08:39:20-08:00","id":1190994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184157-wraith20-backer-errata-thread?p=1190912#post1190912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p 161 &amp;quot;If the target dies or is Soulforged while in the Shadowlands, the Proctor\u2019s Shadow gains 10 temporary Angst. <b>If she dies, she automatically becomes a Spectre.</b>&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Unclear language.<br /> <br /> Unsure if the sentence is suggesting that the Proctor wraith becomes a Spectre if they die, or if that the Proctor becomes a Spectre in addition to gaining 10 temporary Angst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Escher's Stair (Level 3 initiate Pandemonium) has a similar confusion in its last sentence. Does the Haunter risk gaining 4 angst or the target of the Art?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T09:52:28-08:00","id":1191022,"title":"","content":"And in the &quot;All Arcanoi use only two attributes&quot; vein...<br /> <br /> Phantasm uses Strength, Charisma, Manipulation, Perception, and Intelligence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T10:14:35-08:00","id":1191030,"title":"","content":"Phantasm 5: Oneirataxia <br /> <br /> This doesn't give any angst at all?! Even for driving a victim into permanent catatonia? Surely a sentence was omitted. <br /> <br /> From Guildbook:Sandmen page 51:<br /> &quot;... and the wraith's Shadow gains 1 point of Permanent Angst when the mortal goes mad.&quot;<br /> <br /> I suspect that sentence got accidentally omitted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T13:43:45-08:00","id":1191109,"title":"","content":"Usury 4: Oblivion's Seal<br /> <br /> &quot;...The player spends any amount of Pathos and rolls Charisma + Usury (difficulty of 3 + the total number of characters to be bound). Each other bound party agrees to the terms and that player spends 1 Pathos.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does this not work with NPC's, just PC's? I can't tell which is the player of the Usurer and which is a fellow player at the table. The nouns all seem a bit confusing. <br /> <br /> If you can use it with NPC's, who really don't have players, might we consider something like this: &quot;The Usurer spends any amount of Pathos and rolls Charisma + Usury (difficulty of 3+ the total number of targets to be bound). Each other bound party agrees to the terms and that target spends 1 Pathos.&quot;<br /> <br /> At least, I think that would help clear up the intent. Alternately I completely misunderstood how this art functions, but if so it still shows the confused wording.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T16:45:50-08:00","id":1191161,"title":"","content":"Don't know if you'll call that an error:<br /> <br /> p. 213 ANY nonconsensual use of the art allows the subject to resist with his Willpower.<br /> <br /> p. 416 All Puppetry arts can be used on Awakened beings. However, UNLIKE MORTALS, they CAN fight back.<br /> <br /> <br /> Seems like one contradicts the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23863-gothmate","name":"gothmate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T17:14:26-08:00","id":1191167,"title":"","content":"Page 115 has a sidebar with Freebie Point Costs for character creation. <br /> We probably need one for Shadow creation somewhere in the Shadow chapter. It's a bit vague what things cost (other than Thorns)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T20:57:20-08:00","id":1191224,"title":"","content":"Page 236, top of the right column: &quot;Any art that normally would cause the wraith to gain Angst instead subtracts it during Catharsis, and the same goes if the result is a failure or botch.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm confused. So if a wraith in Catharsis uses an Arcanos that normally gives Angst, he loses that much Angst, and then if he fails the roll for that Arcanos he loses that much Angst again? If he botches an Arcanos roll that doesn't grant Angst, does he risk losing Angst on that botch?<br /> <br /> (Next morning...)<br /> Okay, so having slept on this, maybe this just references the earlier rule that Shadows hate failure and take a point of Angst when they fail a roll. If so, this is at best redundant and worse, confusing. But I'm still not sure if I'm getting the intent of the sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12023,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","user":"MMSPR","date":". 03-03-2018, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T21:49:20-08:00","id":1191243,"title":"","content":"I know everyone has been posting the typos they see as they go. This is what I have found in Book One. They've probably all been spotted and listed earlier, but just in case one got missed, here is what I have found:<br /> <br /> pg. 44, left column: &quot;The two main classes of items in the Underworld are relics and Artifacts. relics come from the Skinlands.&quot; = sentence needs to be capitalized<br /> pg. 47 sidebar: &quot;Originally created to hold only the most dangerous enemies of the empire, the chains weree long since repurposed....&quot; = two e's on 'were'<br /> pg. 47 right column: &quot;In a few instances. coffles of thralls....&quot; = period should be a comma<br /> pg. 48 left column: &quot;...worn by those in service to the isle.&quot; = I suspect 'isle' should be capitalized. It is the Isle of Sorrows afterall<br /> pg 49 left column: &quot;They may be things she loved in life: living relatives and loved ones, places where treasured events happened, such as the tools she used in satisfying work.&quot; = This last clause would either work better as the first clause or should be rephrased, replacing 'such as' with &quot;or'.<br /> pg. 62 left column: &quot;Each new addition to the Council is briefed on what her real duties are and where here real loyalties must lie....&quot; = misspelled 'here' for 'her'<br /> pg. 66 left column: &quot;Some are cults are personality,...&quot; = Probably should be 'Some are cults of personality....&quot;<br /> pg. 70 right column: &quot;...the chaos of being the receptacle of untold numbers of souls every deal.&quot; = Probably 'deal' was mistaken for 'day'<br /> pg. 71 right column, last line &quot;... even if the long-term consequences not always desirable.&quot; = Should be 'are not always&quot;<br /> pg. 80 right column: under the last line of The Salon there is a reference to the Grim Legion's purview. Probably should be the Iron Legion.<br /> pg. 149 left column: &quot;Some arts, particularly those that coerce or destroy, also allow the user's Shadow to batten on temporary Angst.&quot; = I think 'batten' should be 'fatten'<br /> pg. 154 right column: in the top paragraph the pronouns used switch from feminine to masculine halfway through the paragraph<br /> pg. 168 left column under Factions: &quot;Mostly, though, it's because Alchemists try offset their bad reputation....&quot; = Should be 'try to offset'<br /> pg. 195 right column, first line: &quot;...furniture, the chair becomes will have a scratch or burn mark....&quot; = Should be 'the chair he becomes'<br /> pg. 206 sidebar: &quot;Storytellers and players are alike are encouraged....&quot; = Remove the second 'are' from this sentence<br /> pg. 211 left column under Tableau of Terror: &quot;Some Sandmen have made special study of the art of Phantasmagoria (see below)....&quot; = This should be '(see above)' as Phantasmagoria was listed earlier.<br /> pg. 221 left column: &quot;and it is neither shy or ashamed....&quot; = Probably should be 'shy nor ashamed' <br /> pg. 221 left column: &quot;No one else can here its whispered asides,....&quot; = Misspelled 'here' instead of 'hear'<br /> pg. 225 right column at the top: the word 'doesn't ' is repeated twice on the second line<br /> pg. 229 right column: &quot;When it is in control, the Perfectionist will take every example to criticize whatever or whoever catches his eye.&quot; Seems like 'example' should be 'opportunity'<br /> pg. 234 both columns: Both paragraphs at the top of each column are mistakenly split into second paragraphs <br /> pg. 234 right column: &quot;Annys docs this, deciding on the Dark Passion....&quot; = The word 'docs' should be the word 'does'<br /> pg. 235 left column: &quot;The Shadow can offer up to five extra dice to any single roll. This is the most likely to be accepted when it's life or death....&quot; = Probably should drop the word 'the' and read &quot;This is most likely....&quot;<br /> pg. 235 right column: Under 'Botching a roll when the Shadow is dominant:' it uses the phrase &quot;...one rolled above the number of successes.&quot; This seems to be a throw-back to second edition rules, as any successes on any dice in the 20th Anniversary edition rules means it isn't a botch.<br /> pg. 241 right column: &quot;Items can be plucked from thin air, the action can teleport form place to place....&quot; = The word 'form' should be replaced with the word 'from'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T09:56:29-08:00","id":1191372,"title":"","content":"p.221 &quot;No one else can here its whispered asides&quot;, correct is &quot;hear&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23863-gothmate","name":"gothmate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T13:57:02-08:00","id":1191444,"title":"","content":"I know it has been mentioned that an index will be added into the final version. I presume the character sheet(s) will also be as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23872-doryna","name":"Doryna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23872_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T00:44:48-08:00","id":1191565,"title":"","content":"These I\u2019ve noted so far <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Page numbers as per pdf)<br /> <br /> P. 4 \u201cBut soon this *will* one will<br /> <br /> P. 8 \u201dThere\u2019s naught I can *dif* you let your shadow rule\u201d<br /> <br /> P.30 \u201cThese wretches will take what they can *frm* you.\u201d<br /> <br /> P.33 \u201c*Bute* enough illusions.\u201d<br /> <br /> P.49 \u201d To look *ino* the eyes of those you left behind? Can you stand to return *hoome*?\u201d<br /> <br /> P.51 \u201dIn her line of work she is never short *ofcash*.\u201d<br /> <br /> P.59 \u201dI am *t he* Incarnation of Death\u201d<br /> <br /> P.83 The Player: *NoStoryteller* can function without players, the actors in the drama they<br /> create together.<br /> <br /> P.85 \u201dBut despite its horrors and excesses, most wraiths readily concede it\u2019s better *that* the<br /> visible alternative.\u201d<br /> <br /> P.92 \u201cAs with any history or great piece of artwork, not every detail is portrayed or<br /> examined to the *nth* degree.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4427-malfean_sleepover","name":"Malfean_Sleepover","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4427_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T02:20:20-08:00","id":1191579,"title":"","content":"p.234 She spends three more points on the Trick of the Light Thorn, knowing how heavily (it shouldn't have a paragraph here)<br /> Robin relies on reading others\u2019 body language and what that says about their intentions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23863-gothmate","name":"gothmate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T05:44:16-08:00","id":1191601,"title":"","content":"p.230 &quot;A wraith\u2019s Angst rating is indicative of the amount of negative emotional energy she is carrying a round with her. (extra space in &quot;around&quot; word)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23863-gothmate","name":"gothmate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T20:10:25-08:00","id":1191819,"title":"","content":"Page 236: Relicforging. The second paragraph calls out Status 3 (Artificer's Guild) as a prerequisite to knowing how to relic forge. This seems like it should be Alchemist's Guild status instead. Why would a unique talent among the Alchemist's, whose use of Flux allows numerous effects over relics require such a high rating in another guild to Relic Forge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T20:25:40-08:00","id":1191823,"title":"","content":"Page 384 Relic Vehicle chart does not list the Pathos cost for activation for any of the vehicles listed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T22:05:12-08:00","id":1191839,"title":"","content":"p. 169 &quot;The player spends 2 Pathos and rolls Dexterity + Flux (<b>normal difficulty in the Shadowlands</b>, difficulty 6 in the Tempest, and difficulty 5 in the Labyrinth).&quot;<br /> <br /> Normal difficulty being...what, exactly? Especially since the TNs for the Tempest and the Labyrinth are listed but no number is given for the Shadowlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T22:52:41-08:00","id":1191848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184157-wraith20-backer-errata-thread?p=1191839#post1191839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p. 169 &quot;The player spends 2 Pathos and rolls Dexterity + Flux (<b>normal difficulty in the Shadowlands</b>, difficulty 6 in the Tempest, and difficulty 5 in the Labyrinth).&quot;<br /> <br /> Normal difficulty being...what, exactly? Especially since the TNs for the Tempest and the Labyrinth are listed but no number is given for the Shadowlands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly enough, reference difficulty is supposed to be 6 if not explicitly stated, but they mentioned it for the Tempest...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T07:02:43-08:00","id":1191910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184157-wraith20-backer-errata-thread?p=1191839#post1191839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p. 169 &quot;The player spends 2 Pathos and rolls Dexterity + Flux (<b>normal difficulty in the Shadowlands</b>, difficulty 6 in the Tempest, and difficulty 5 in the Labyrinth).&quot;<br /> <br /> Normal difficulty being...what, exactly? Especially since the TNs for the Tempest and the Labyrinth are listed but no number is given for the Shadowlands.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Presumably in the Shadowlands the difficulty is the Shroud rating (I think).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T07:52:55-08:00","id":1191926,"title":"","content":"Okay, so here is what I have seen in Book 2. As before, I suspect most of this has been mentioned elsewhere, but just in case, I'd hate to miss something, so apologies for any repetition.<br /> <br /> page 253 left column: &quot;The players may portray the heroes of a given chronicle, but it's the Storyteller who plays the villains, the noble allies, the informants and bit parts, and all the rest of the world entire.&quot; = the phrase 'world entire' is a bit awkward in English. It might have been the goal, as it is a bit poetic, but it isn't natural.<br /> page 265 right column, under Wraith vs. Spectres: &quot;The conflict can here can be as simple as Spectres wanting into a citadel during a Maelstrom while the wraith wants to keep them out.&quot; = the preposition 'into' is a bit awkward here. 'to get into' seems a bit less awkward perhaps<br /> page 267 right column: &quot;Maybe one side brings in powerful allies, or change tactics from sneak attacks to full on assaults,&quot; = the single third person subject 'one side' needs the verb to be 'changes'. And the phrase 'full on' should probably be 'full-on' with a hyphen.<br /> page 268 left column, last sentence: &quot;The Circle works happily for the Hierarchy as enforcers of the Dictum Mortuum, and its good at what it does.&quot; = In this case the word 'its' is the contraction for 'it is' and should have the apostrophe so that i reads 'it's' (I get this wrong more than I get it right so I hope I'm correct in this case)<br /> page 270 right column near the bottom: &quot;You can also try &quot;Protect my lover (Hope),&quot; wherein the wraith wants to and helps the lover succeed...&quot; = I suspect that this should be either 'the wraith wants to help the lover succeed' or 'the wraith helps the lover succeed' but as it stands I think it kind of merges the two into a muddle<br /> page 281 right column: Halfway thru the paragraph the Reaper pronouns changed from 'she' to 'he'. Likewise the Enfant's pronouns changed from 'her' to 'their'.<br /> page 282 right column at the top: same thing. The Reaper goes from being a 'her' to a 'their',<br /> page 283 left column at the bottom: &quot;The empire employs specialists that aggressively work to distort or suppress evidence from such incidents,...&quot; = More of a question. Since this is the Empire of Stygia, should 'empire' be capitalized?<br /> page 286 right column: &quot;Maelstrom winds behave like the winds of Skinlands storms in terms of battering structures and turning loose debris into dangerous projectiles, but they are also pose far more insidious threats.&quot; = need to remove the word 'are' from this<br /> page 288 left column near the bottom: &quot;A cemetery poisoned with disdain and empty beer bottles can make a far worse Haunt than the basement of an old row home where once upon a time, a small child was locked in the dark by her friends.&quot; = either the clause 'once upon a time' needs to be set off on both sides with commas, or not at all. So either this sentence needs a second comma after the word 'where' or it needs none. Kind of a matter of choice. <br /> page 297 left column: &quot;Indeed, scholars of the phenomenon assert that trying to define exactly what Transcendence is a bit like trying to precisely qualify a notion like zen....&quot; = the word 'is' is trying and failing to do double duty here. You could repeat the word 'is' twice, but that always looks awkward even if it is grammatically correct. Might I suggest simply dropping the words 'exactly what', and if you want to keep the word 'exactly ' then place it before the word 'define'<br /> page 298 right column: &quot;Aspirants sometimes add their own thoughts and experiences to the text when making new copies, for one, not to mention discreetly alter or even remove passages they consider erroneous. &quot; = For starters, I would say 'for example' instead of 'for one'. I would also make the words 'alter' and 'remove' into 'altering' and 'removing'.<br /> page 302 left column at the bottom: &quot;Requirements found in individual sections below.&quot; = Except there is no Merit section below. I wish there was, as Wraith always had the coolest merits, but I get that for space they may not be able to be reprinted. Might I suggest that the word 'Merits' be removed if there will be no Merits section.<br /> page 303 right column: &quot;Improving Physical Attributes or the Appearance Trait is very different for the Restless than for the living.&quot; = It's less awkward if you say 'than it is for the living.'<br /> page 308 left column: &quot;Each success restores 1 Willpower point, up the character's normal maximum.&quot; = should be 'up to the character's normal maximum'<br /> page 308 left column: &quot;That doesn't mean it doesn't happen, of course, but it does mean an attacker tends to work as indirectly as possible in order to make it hard to trace back her.&quot; = Probably best as 'back to her'. <br /> page 308 sidebar: &quot;This rule should not reduce a Fetter rating to zero - even if looks completely different,....&quot; = should read 'even if it looks completely different'<br /> page 311 left column: &quot;Referred to as Slumber, this state is a first and foremost a restorative one for an injured wraith.&quot; = There's an extra article in this. 'this state is first and foremost'. Drop the 'a' before 'first'<br /> page 320 left column: Under Lift/Break the phrase &quot;Strengthtable&quot; needs a space. Also the reference to the die roll seems unusual. Maybe 'dice roll'? Maybe you meant it to refer to a single die, although most people roll dice as apposed to a die for strength,<br /> page 323 right column near the bottom: &quot;...attempts to track the Restless or Spectres without benefit of an appropriate Arcanoi starts at difficulty 8.&quot; = should read 'Arcanos' or remove the word 'an'<br /> <br /> I have a few other concerns on system that I'll leave below that are not typos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T08:00:50-08:00","id":1191927,"title":"","content":"The level 4 Castigate art &quot;Cooling the Blood&quot; may have a temporary effect in duration measured in scenes, but if the Pardoner nails his roll and reduces all Dark Passions temporarily to zero, the Shadow loses a Permanent Angst. Wow! So, the next day the Pardoner does this again, and the next day again.... <br /> <br /> What happens when the Shadow has no Permanent Angst? That seems amazingly powerful. <br /> <br /> Question: Is this okay? Or can the Pardoner maybe not reduce permanent Angst below 1? This would be the time to add a restriction if Permanent Angst zero is an unintended consequence, because I have a player that will totally jump on this loophole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T08:06:11-08:00","id":1191928,"title":"","content":"Page 303 speaks of reducing the cost of Arcanoi with Mentors and Guild Status. <br /> In the first paragraph at the top of the right-hand column, it says that the Background can be rolled at difficulty 6, but the cost can't be reduced below 1.<br /> In the third paragraph in the right-hand column, it says that the Background can be rolled at difficulty 8, but the cost can't be reduced below half cost. <br /> This feels a bit confusing (at least to me), Does this apply to arts that are higher than the level of the Mentor or Guild Background?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T08:10:32-08:00","id":1191930,"title":"","content":"Resolving Passions and Fetters both require a Willpower roll at a difficulty of 5+the original level of the trait, and needs a number of successes equal to the original level of the trait.<br /> <br /> So... a 5 point Passion or Fetter would require a Willpower roll at difficulty 10 with 5 successes needed to resolve, which would be near impossible to ever roll. This seems a bit extreme. Might that difficulty of the Willpower roll be +4? That is at least a difficulty 9 roll with 5 successes needed, a crazy longshot but at least in the realm of imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T08:12:56-08:00","id":1191931,"title":"","content":"Page 316 says that if you have a Specialty, 10's count as two successes. On page 125 it says that Specialties allow you to reroll 10's. <br /> I gather that the new WoD books are going with double successes. Probably 125 needs to be corrected rather than 316.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T08:17:41-08:00","id":1191935,"title":"","content":"Page 316, under &quot;Activate Arcanoi&quot; in the left column and under &quot;Power a Relic&quot; in the right column both mention a 'per-turn rating' for Pathos expenditure.<br /> ???<br /> I assume that this was a copy-and-paste error from Vampire, where those guys actually have a vitae-per-turn expenditure limit. Admittedly I can be pretty unobservant, but in all my years of running Wraith (and I ran it the week it came out) I simply do not remember ever reading of a per-turn-limit on Pathos expenditure, including in this book. Have I just missed this at every single reading? If I have, I will crawl into the Labyrinth in abject shame, and beg you to give me a page reference and accept my apology for running this wrong for over 20 years. If I haven't, these references to per-turn-limits need to be removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T08:21:28-08:00","id":1191937,"title":"","content":"Page 316 - Heal requires a Stamina + Survival roll<br /> Page 323 - Track requires a Perception + Survival roll<br /> Spectres have to roll survival too I note. <br /> <br /> Survival is not on the character sheet<br /> <br /> One the other hand, on page 331 Dodging requires a Dexterity + Athletics roll.<br /> <br /> Seems to me that the needed Ability 'Survival' was replaced by the unneeded Ability 'Dodge' on the character sheet. This seems an easy typo to fix on the character sheet. Just swap in Survival for Dodge.<br /> <br /> Better yet, swap Leadership over to the talents in place of Dodge and then swap Survival in for Leadership. Then it meshes with the other WoD games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12023,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","user":"MMSPR","date":". 03-05-2018, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T08:23:26-08:00","id":1191938,"title":"","content":"Page 318 and 329 refer to spending Pathos to 'heal' a relic vehicle, relic or Artifact,<br /> <br /> Is there a system for this, or do you just spend the Pathos, touch the relic, and heal the damage like you would yourself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T08:25:40-08:00","id":1191940,"title":"","content":"Page 330 under the heading The Tempest says that there is a +1 difficulty to Mental rolls made in the Tempest. Makes sense.<br /> <br /> ...except...<br /> <br /> Argos is a Mental roll. Tempestos and Tempest Weaving have mental rolls as well in their descriptions.<br /> <br /> Might those three Arcanoi be exceptions to the &quot;+1 difficulty to Mental rolls in the Tempest&quot; rule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T08:42:34-08:00","id":1191946,"title":"","content":"Page 339<br /> Crossbows take 5 rounds to reload, no excpetions, but with a successful Dex+Firearm roll you can shoot, reload, and shoot again with a Matchlock rifle in a single round.<br /> <br /> ... seriously?<br /> <br /> A handspan crossbow fires at roughly half the rate of a longbow. Or every other round, if you allow bows to shoot every round. There's a few good youtube videos on this, btw, and it only admittedly applies to the handspan crossbow, which has a light pull and doesn't have as much strength as larger crossbows. But 5 rounds seems a bit slow for crossbows.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, paper cartridges allowed quicker reloading of flintlocks, but in no way could you do 2 shots in a round as I understand it. 1 shot every 12 seconds seems to be the fastest I have seen anyone do it on youtube, and that assumes the right equipment, namely paper cartridges.<br /> <br /> So here's a thought:<br /> I think archaic firearms should probable be once every 5 rounds, with successes on the Dex+Firearm roll reducing that, maybe even down to every other round at the quickest (it takes one full round of reloading at the quickest).<br /> I think maybe a similar rule for Crossbows, with 5 rounds to reload, and a Dex+Athletics roll to reduce this time, again to a minimum of every other round, taking a minimum of one full round to reload.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T09:56:10-08:00","id":1191978,"title":"","content":"The Spectres chapter (pg 348) references specific Lifesight, Deathsight, and Sharpened Senses powers (i.e. Discern Weakness). These seem to be lacking throughout the book I think... can't seem to find a system on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T13:43:31-08:00","id":1192047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fspardoner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184157-wraith20-backer-errata-thread?p=1185440#post1185440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the page 236 says &amp;quot;In order for the Shadow to take control of a character, the Shadow and the Psyche face off against one another. The Shadow spends a point of temporary Angst and rolls on her adjusted temporary Angst rating. The Psyche may resist by rolling her permanent Willpower, plus any Eidolon dice she may possess (see \u201cEidolon,\u201d p. 143).&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> And on the page 230 says &amp;quot;When a wraith\u2019s temporary Angst exceeds her Willpower, the Shadow can attempt to usurp control of the Corpus by means of a Catharsis roll (see p. 236)&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> For the sake of clarity, is there a need for the temporary Angst level to be greater than the psyche's permanent Willpower to enable the Catharsis roll? If the wraith has Willpower 10, the character will it be immune to Catharsis?</div> </div> </div> </div>This problem existed in first and second edition, and I had a player buy up to ten Willpower with the hope that he'd never face Catharsis. So I house-ruled that when Temp Angst equaled or exceeded WP Catharsis could kick in. <br /> <br /> It would be nice if this new edition tweaked things just enough to keep from needing that house rule. &quot;When a wraith' temporary Angst equals or exceeds...&quot; would make a great fix to the text. Seems like erata to me when the rules need this to work as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T17:51:13-08:00","id":1192097,"title":"","content":"p. 177 The Solictor's faction names are not italicized. This is inconsistent with the other Guild faction write-ups since all of their faction names are italicized.<br /> <br /> So, the following names need to be italicized:<br /> <br /> Spoke of Leo<br /> Spoke of Aries<br /> Spoke of Capricorn<br /> Spoke of Taurus<br /> Spoke of Pisces","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T23:14:03-08:00","id":1192156,"title":"","content":"p. 178 &quot;The number of successes determines the complexity and strength of desire <b>Suppress</b> can remove.&quot;<br /> <br /> Incorrect power name. The word should be &quot;Excise&quot;.<br /> <br /> p. 180 &quot;Most elder Solicitors maintain entire <b>coteries</b> of Passion-bound wraiths, ensuring a constant supply of Pathos.&quot;<br /> <br /> Possibly incorrect gameline terminology from Vampire? Replace with &quot;circles&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 03-06-2018, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T06:58:01-08:00","id":1192237,"title":"","content":"p.68 has descriptions of the Ferrymen's immense power and their equipment (and their great secret), but no actual mechanics are given in the book.<br /> <br /> p.89 Describing the Coup, &quot;The Alchemists in turn pulled strings within the Guilds to foment a rebellion.&quot; But their description on pp.167-168 says they were outlawed centuries before and &quot;They weren\u2019t invited to sign the Compact of Guilds, much less to join the revolt against Charon. Indeed, some aided Stygia, seeing the chance to pay back the Artificers for centuries of persecution.&quot;<br /> <br /> p.91 says &quot;...but no Oracles were put to the forge. Their Guildhalls were not raided and their wealth was not seized.&quot; Their desc. on p.163 says &quot;Elder Guildwraiths held their tongues despite knowing the price to come \u2014 and, when the Legions responded with sword and barrow-flame, offered themselves as sacrifice.&quot;<br /> <br /> The bookmarks for the Guilds are out of order, with Oracles swapped with Alchemists, Mnemoi swapped with Monitors, and Sandmen swapped with Haunters.<br /> <br /> p.189 and p.375 mention Gaunts, but they aren't defined in the Lexicon.<br /> <br /> p.179 and p.188 mention Derangements, uncapitalized on p.179, but they're never defined.<br /> <br /> p.405 has mummies interacting with the Restless Dead, but their aren't given in the Awakened section.<br /> <br /> p.474 In the Pigment sidebar, &quot;While the smoker receives intermittent Lifesight and Death in this state&quot; should be Deathsight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T14:29:12-08:00","id":1192395,"title":"","content":"p. 183 &quot;The player rolls Charisma + Keening (difficulty 7), with the number of successes indicating the depth and duration of the feeling evoked: <b>1 day per success for one of the Quick</b>, one hour per success for a wraith.&quot;<br /> <br /> So that would suggest that you can use Keening ** (Mood Music) in the Skinlands, but no reference is made at all on how the Shroud difficulty would factor in, if at all. Additionally, this is the only Keening power that makes reference to being able to use on the Quick and thus in the Skinlands, while the other powers make no such reference.<br /> <br /> p. 186 &quot;When a wraith is subject to any Lifeweb art that isn\u2019t immediately obvious through other means, <b>he may make a Perception + Awareness roll</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> No Difficulty TN is listed. While yes, under the general Systems heading, the Difficulty TNs are listed there and vary depending on the locations of Fetters...however, this roll is about the Monitor using Lifeweb on themselves to check a different wraith is using Lifeweb on them. Which I would think would require a fixed TN because the wraith isn't trying to use Lifeweb through the usual barriers of Underworld planes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 03-07-2018, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T23:18:53-08:00","id":1192529,"title":"","content":"So here are the things I found in Book 3. As I said on my reviews of Books 1 &amp; 2, I am sure that I missed some things, and I know that I am surely repeating things that have been said before, not to be dogmatic but because, in completeness, we don't want to miss anything. So here is the list I have from book 3:<br /> <br /> page 344 left column near top: &quot;Birthed in agony, they desired only an end to their pain even at the cost of all existence.&quot; = I would put a comma after the word 'pain'<br /> page 344 left column: &quot;While ultimately repulsed, they managed to infect the very darkness itself to rise up against the defending Legions.&quot; = Is 'infect' the best word in this instance?<br /> page 345 sidebar, last sentence: &quot;... in for far trouble than they're ready for.&quot; = Probably 'in for far greater trouble than they're ready for.' Or perhaps 'far more trouble'<br /> page 348 right column: There is a break in the second paragraph under Lifesight<br /> page 349: &quot;Each extra success you roll reduces the target's Willpower score by 1;&quot; = I assume based upon the following sentences that this is actually Permanent Willpower. Usually I would expect it to be temporary Willpower, but since the follow-up sentence references Permanent Willpower, I suppose this must be Permanent as well. It would be clearer if this sentence specified Permanent Willpower.<br /> page 355 left column: The art Empower refers to basic Abilities. Those don't exist anymore.<br /> page 355 right column: Under Lurking Presence it says &quot;While this art is in effect, subjects who view you are not affected by the Fog, as appropriate to their Willpower ratings.&quot; = So I can't tell if the word &quot;not&quot; was put in there incorrectly or if the phrase 'as appropriate to their Willpower Ratings' was put in their needlessly, since, if they are not affected by it, their Willpower ratings are moot.<br /> page 356 right column last sentence: ...and may use Navigate for basic maneuverability...&quot; = What is Navigate? Is that a skill or an art in another Arcanos? I can't find that one anywhere. It seems a bit like Maelstrom Navigation, the basic Argos ability from Great War<br /> page 360 left column: &quot;Spend 5 Angst and roll Manipulation+Leadership; each success represents one Shade that appears, to a maximum offive Shades.&quot; = the words 'of five' need a space between them.<br /> page 366 right column: The first paragraph under the heading &quot;Horror&quot; has been broken into two paragraphs <br /> page 368: right column: The paragraph under the sub-heading &quot;A-Viking&quot; has been broken into two paragraphs<br /> page 370 sidebar: &quot;A destructive, treacherous Spectrecharacter is great,....&quot; = The words 'Spectre character' need a space between them<br /> page 371 right column: &quot;If a player is excited about turning her wraith character into a Spectre, she isencouraged to discuss it....&quot; = The words 'is encouraged' need a space between them<br /> page 372 right column near the top: &quot;If the other characters figure out what's going on by themselves, that's one thing and they should certainly encouraged to react appropriately.&quot; = I would put a comma after the word 'thing', and the word 'be' needs to come after the word 'certainly'<br /> page 374 right column under Shades: &quot;A Shade character has access only to Dark Arcanoi. Y;ou may allocate five dots among them as you choose.&quot; = the word 'You' has a typo<br /> page 375 left column under Backgrounds: The word &quot;Sspectre&quot; has an extra 's' in it. Also, there is a reference to the Wealth background that apparently no longer exists.<br /> page 377 left column: Arcanoi Basic Abilities appear on the table<br /> page 378 sidebar: &quot;But just because they believe it exists doesn't mean they're pursue it-&quot; = the contraction &quot;they're&quot; should be &quot;they'll&quot;<br /> page 379 left column last line: &quot;The points function just like a Spectre's Angst pool,....&quot; = I wonder if this should say &quot;just like a Shadow's Angst pool&quot;, since the Psyche of a Spectre is more easily compared to the Shadow of a wraith<br /> page 387 sidebar: &quot;...the rabbi shouldn't out to screw over the Circle, not deliberately.&quot; = Probably should read 'shouldn't set out to screw over'<br /> page 391 left column at the bottom: &quot;...and there's no telling what the individual Shadows will do to get the Psyche sin trouble.&quot; = the word 'sin' should be 'in'<br /> page 393 right column: &quot;A Risen who chooses to go back isn't always successful in her driving mission, and not every mission results on a Resolved Passion or Fetter.&quot; = should probably read 'results in a Resolved Passion or Fetter.'<br /> page 395 sidebar: 'Endurance' should be replaced with 'Stamina'<br /> page 395 right column: There is another reference to the non-existent Wealth background<br /> page 395 right column: Here it says that a wraith needs 1 level of Puppetry and 2 of the three Lifeweb, Inhabit, and Embody. Page 389 says that they need 3 dots in Puppetry and one dot in each of the other three. These two pages (389 &amp; 395) give different prerequisites for Rising.<br /> page 396 under Fascinate: &quot;It a focused, distilled version of that obsession....&quot; = should read 'It is a focused, distilled version....'<br /> page 396 under Fascinate: &quot;Instead, it serves a mechanism for persuasion....&quot; = should probably read 'Instead, it serves as a mechanism for persuasion....'<br /> page 397 at the top of the page: &quot;A target can't receive more than one Driving Urge,....&quot; = The name of this power is no longer Driving Urge; it is Overriding Behavior.<br /> page 405: &quot;But there's people, and then there's people, and then there are the things that either used to be people or never were,....&quot; = Was it intentional to repeat the first clause? I'm not against it if it was intentional. Reads a bit quirky.<br /> page 407 left column: &quot;There are those who do it in exchange for protection of their Fetters, or favors done their living loved ones.&quot; = Maybe it reads better 'favors done for their living loved ones.'<br /> page 408 left column bottom: &quot;While for many years, the PRW worked with what were called Ectoplasmic Converter Engines,....&quot; = Normally this book uses far less commas than I would (a matter of taste), but in this instance the comma after the word 'years' doesn't belong.<br /> page 407 sidebar: The sidebar just ends mid-sentence. Also... should that be a Perception + Awareness roll (or Alertness even), or is it just straight Perception?<br /> page 409 right column at the bottom: There is a reference to True Faith, but there is no system for True Faith in this book. This was not the only reference to True Faith. It also appears on page 445 in the first full paragraph.<br /> page 410 left column: &quot;The Arcanoi listings for the sample vampires below match vampiric Disciplines to those Arcanoi that arc most similar.&quot; = The word 'arc' should be 'are'<br /> page 410 right column: &quot;Most also possess the Discipline Auspex....&quot; = The previous line says 'Discipline of Thaumaturgy', which personally I think sounds better. 'Discipline of Auspex' probably sounds a bit smoother.<br /> page 412 right column near top: &quot;Humans who view one of these nine-foot monsters, or indeed any Garou in Crinos, usually full into delirious fright.&quot; = the word 'full' should be 'fall'<br /> page 415 left column near the top: &quot;...changeling cantrips arc less about brute force than they are about trickery,....&quot; = The word 'arc' should be 'are'<br /> page 417 under Outrage: &quot;She can, however, set the material in his pockets alight, and let him deal that as he may.&quot; = should read 'and let him deal with that as he may.'<br /> page 422 under the Kraken: I think the phrase is 'dwarfs the largest ship'<br /> page 425 Sweeny's Pride: &quot;This unassuming straight razor, with a finely honed blade and mother-of-pearl inlay in the oak handle. appears fairly innocuous.&quot; = The period after 'handle' should be a comma<br /> page 425 Emperor's Nightingale: &quot;It flies at a slow, but steady and unbroken pace so that its owner can follow,....&quot; = Either put a comma after the word 'unbroken' or get rid of the comma after the word 'slow'<br /> page 427 right column at the bottom: The sentence that begins with &quot;they can fly at 2x normal walking pace,...&quot; needs to be capitalized<br /> page 428 Bloodwebs: The sentence that begins with &quot;anyone hit with a Bloodweb....&quot; needs to be capitalized. <br /> page 428 Bloodwebs: Sometimes a singular Bloodweb is referred to by the pronoun 'they' and sometimes by 'it'<br /> page 429 right column at the bottom: This is the only place that the ability &quot;Dodge&quot; appears, the irony being that in the combat section &quot;Athletics&quot; is used to Dodge. As has been suggested, this should be replaced here with the ability &quot;Athletics&quot; and the game brought closer inline with other WoD games in getting rid of the overly narrow skill Dodge.<br /> page 431 Maggot Revolver: The sentence that begins with &quot;Based on a Colt Anaconda....&quot; has no verb.<br /> page 431 Maggot Revolver: &quot;Rather than shooting bullets, however, the gun launches revolting creatures called Shadow Maggots, one maggot is delivered on each success on a damage roll....&quot; = This is two sentences; a period or semi-colon should appear between 'Shadow Maggots' and 'one', replacing the comma that is there.<br /> page 434 left column: &quot;The p'o, on the other hand, represents the part of the spirit that identifies most with the physical remains of the wraith and to the physical world.&quot; = I would drop the word 'to' at the end of the sentence and say 'of the wraith and the physical world.'<br /> page 434 left column at the bottom: &quot;But many choose to live in Shadowlands, adapting to their new situation as best they can.&quot; = Usually it would be 'to live in the Shadowlands'<br /> page 434 right column top: &quot;Jade reapers can be found expanding as far as Polynesia as the emperor extends his influence,....&quot; = Should we capitalize the word 'emperor' here, since it is THE emperor?<br /> page 434 right column bottom: &quot;From the perspective of citizens in Yellow Springs,....&quot; = Might read better as 'citizens in the Yellow Springs'<br /> page 436 right column bottom: &quot;Fearful of death and of the many enemies he sent to the Shadowlands. Qin Shihuang started a two-pronged strategy.&quot; = The period between 'Shadowlands' and 'Qin' should be a comma<br /> page 438 left column: &quot;And as such he as reigned, though Maelstrom, war, rebellion and even peace, ever since.&quot; = Probably the word 'though' should be 'through'<br /> page 440 left column under Ti Yu: the name Feng-tu should be capitalized as Feng-Tu to be consistent with earlier references<br /> page 450 left column: &quot;Before the Heretics came, the wraiths of the Flayed Lands only knew one way to harvest Pathos; the sacrifices made by the human priests.&quot; = Should that be a colon instead of a semi-colon?<br /> page 453: In the last line the 'Mla Watu' are misspelled as 'Mia Watu'<br /> page 454: Sinkinda should be spelled Sikinda to be consistent with the rest of the book I think<br /> page 456 at the top: The first and second sentences are not separated by a period. 'themBut' appears<br /> page 457 left column: 'Les Imvisibles' is misspelled in the second full paragraph<br /> page 457 left column: in the same paragraph &quot;iIsland&quot; is likewise misspelled<br /> page 457 right column bottom: The second to last paragraph ends quite suddenly (and mysteriously, too)<br /> page 458 right column at the top: &quot;With this power, the Scholar an issue a single command....&quot; = should read 'the Scholar can issue a single command'<br /> page 459 right column: &quot;If the Artisan is attempting to imbue an Arcanos power, it costs a Willpower point plus another Pathos for the level of the Arcanos power being imbued.&quot; = Should that read &quot;...plus another Pathos per level of the Arcanos power being imbued&quot;? I can't quite figure out what 'for the level of the Arcanos power being imbued' means in this sentence<br /> page 461 right column Coax: &quot;To use Coax, rollWay of the Soul....&quot; = There needs to be a space between 'roll' and 'Way'<br /> page 461 right column Alter Demeanor: Charisma + Manipulation roll. Really? I thought that was a typo in the Dark Kingdom of Jade Book<br /> page 461 right column: with the difficulty of the p'o's Angst +4, there is a chance for a difficulty of 14. Seems a bit much<br /> page 463: Too many references to the Great War, to Kinesis, and to Swar instead of Svarga. Under Wraithride there is a Sense Kinesis roll<br /> page 465: Two of the paragraphs in the left column are broken in two<br /> page 466 left column: &quot;And in the European hells, time is not to be wasted, for as long an African wraith remains outside the Bush of Ghosts, his very soul mutates into the dyad soul of a Stygian wraith....&quot; = the word 'dyad' is presumably the word 'dead' misspelled. I would also insert the word as to create the phrase 'as long as'<br /> page 469 sidebar: &quot;Orpheus possesses little knowledge of Stygia, operating exclusively in the Shadowlands and only now slowly starting to scratch the surface of death's mystery.&quot; This sentence feels a bit awkward. Maybe &quot;...Shadowlands, and is only now...&quot;, adding a comma after Shadowlands and the verb 'is'<br /> page 472 right column: &quot;...Orpheus knew skimming was possible, and they ventured into Underworld.&quot; = Maybe they ventured into the Underworld'<br /> page 474: Lifesight and Death = Should be 'Deathsight' I assume<br /> page 476 right column: &quot;Besides espionage, the NSA and through them the CIA and Homeland Security, continues to employ Orpheus for the occasional targeted killing.&quot; = There should be a comma after NSA<br /> page 477 lower sidebar: Bounces back and forth between referring to 'points' and 'dots'. Probably should mostly be 'dots'<br /> page 480 left column near bottom: &quot;While in suspension, the sleeper cannot recover Pathos.&quot; ... &quot;The projecting sleeper recovers Pathos as any other wraith.&quot; = These two sentences seem to totally contradict each other.<br /> page 484 Gossamer Webs: &quot;On successful Brawl attack....&quot; = Probably should say 'On a successful Brawl attack....'<br /> page 484 Spite-fueled Arcanoi: &quot;This is common Stain, and rumors abound....&quot; = should read 'This is a common Stain....' Also might consider capitalizing the F in Spite-fueled in the title<br /> page 486 left column at the bottom: A reference to the Resources background<br /> page 487 left column at the top: &quot;...the projector loses a point of Willpower and take a level of Aggravated damage.&quot; = Should be 'takes a level of Aggravated damage'<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T23:25:40-08:00","id":1192530,"title":"","content":"Doomslayers: Into the Labyrinth says on page 55 that a Wraith using Dark Arcanoi spends pathos instead of Angst. Might we put that little tidbit in the Dark Arcanoi section?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T23:29:35-08:00","id":1192531,"title":"","content":"On page 399 it says &quot;...every use of an Arcanos besides Fascinate or Serendipity gains the user an additional point of Angst.&quot;<br /> <br /> Whoa!<br /> <br /> Does this need to be rephrased?<br /> <br /> I assume that means &quot;Every time an Arcanos other than Fascinate or Serendipity gives Angst, it gives the Risen an additional point of Angst.&quot; Otherwise you'd rack up 10 permanent Angst from innocuous level one arts in no time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T23:31:58-08:00","id":1192532,"title":"","content":"On page 417 the effects of various Arcanoi on non-wraiths is given, but the Forbidden Three aren't listed. Intimation, in particular, seems decidedly needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T23:36:24-08:00","id":1192533,"title":"","content":"On page 339 relic firearms are stated as needing a point of Pathos to activate them for a scene.<br /> On page 428 Soulfire and Souled weapons require Pathos per bullet. <br /> <br /> Is this a mistake, or is the difference between using your own Pathos, which charges the gun for a scene, and a Pathos crystal, which charges the gun for a single shot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T23:38:27-08:00","id":1192535,"title":"","content":"page 461, left column<br /> The Arts of Returning the Favor &amp; Mint Money each have two descriptive paragraphs that are remarkably redundant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T23:39:45-08:00","id":1192536,"title":"","content":"Connaissance is repeatedly referred to in reference to Les Invisbles. <br /> <br /> Please please please please include this one Arcanos that got left out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T23:41:53-08:00","id":1192538,"title":"","content":"The Sea Which Knows No Sun was left out. I find this most curious considering who wrote up the original description in the Player's Guide. Speaking as someone who lived in Papua New Guinea at one point, I appreciated that chapter quite a bit and feel saddened that it got left on the cutting room floor. Is there any way that it can be squeezed in there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T23:44:08-08:00","id":1192539,"title":"","content":"Last thing: <br /> The Orpheus description is surprisingly good. I ran it years ago and vowed &quot;never again&quot;. The story was delightful but the system was a headache. This was a surprisingly good write-up, far better than expected, and well integrated. Bravo! I'm actually interested in running this version and already making plans.<br /> <br /> Any chance of an Orpheus character sheet? They have sufficient differences that I feel compelled to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T23:57:11-08:00","id":1192540,"title":"","content":"On the &quot;All Arcanoi use only two attributes&quot; thread...<br /> <br /> It's a really great idea that simplifies the game. I love it! Any chance of &quot;All Arcanoi&quot; applying to Dark Arcanoi, Risen Arcanoi, Jade Arcanoi, Behest, Displace, and Connaissance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12023-mmspr","name":"MMSPR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T04:56:10-08:00","id":1192581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MMSPR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184157-wraith20-backer-errata-thread?p=1192529#post1192529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">page 466 left column: &quot;And in the European hells, time is not to be wasted, for as long an African wraith remains outside the Bush of Ghosts, his very soul mutates into the dyad soul of a Stygian wraith....&quot; = the word 'dyad' is presumably the word 'dead' misspelled. I would also insert the word as to create the phrase 'as long as'</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;dyad&quot; means having two parts, the Psyche and Shadow, as opposed to the four parts of African ghosts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T08:45:59-08:00","id":1192621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184157-wraith20-backer-errata-thread?p=1192581#post1192581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;dyad&amp;quot; means having two parts, the Psyche and Shadow, as opposed to the four parts of African ghosts.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You are no doubt correct, but this is an errata thread so please only post errata, no answers or explanations. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T17:47:18-08:00","id":1192873,"title":"","content":"p 17 \u2013 Each of the \u201cchapter summaries\u201d (except for \u201cChapter 13: The Dark Kingdoms\u201d and \u201cAppendix: Orpheus\u201d) need a period at the end<br /> p 17, second para of second column (\u201cChapter 11: The Risen\u201d) \u2013 \u201cstorytelling\u201d should be capitalized<br /> p 17, last full para of second column \u2013 \u201cand storytellers don\u2019t railroad players\u201d should be capitalized \u201cStorytellers\u201d<br /> p 18, third full para of first column \u2013 \u201ccalled The Shadow\u201d should be \u201cthe Shadow\u201d (capitalization)<br /> p 18, last para of first column \u2013 \u201chow\u2019d they react\u201d would be better \u201chow they\u2019d react\u201d<br /> p 18, fourth para of second column \u2013 \u201cold newspaper clippings and more\u201d needs a comma, \u201cclippings, and more\u201d<br /> p 19, first full para of first column \u2013 \u201cvariation on the Wraith experience\u201d needs to have the game name in bold<br /> p 19, last full para of first column \u2013 \u201ccollectively called The Underworld\u201d should be \u201cthe Underworld\u201d (capitalization)<br /> p 20, third para of first column \u2013 \u201cbetter that the visible alternative\u201d should be \u201cthan\u201d<br /> p 21, third full para of first column \u2013 \u201cand who knows the wraith\u2019s darkests secrets\u201d would be better as \u201cand it knows\u201d since your wording makes it look like a question?<br /> p 22, second column entry for \u201cOblivion\u201d \u2013 \u201chunger of Entropy\u201d should be lower case \u201centropy\u201d (It\u2019s not a <b>Mage</b> Sphere, is it?)<br /> \u2026same \u2013 \u201c<i>The Great Unmaking</i>\u201d should start lower case \u201c<i>the Great Unmaking</i>\u201d<br /> p 23, first column entry for \u201cStygia\u201d \u2013 needs a period at the end<br /> p 25, first para of second column \u2013 \u201cof the pop charts and the name\u201d needs a comma, \u201ccharts, and the name\u201d<br /> p 26, last para of second column \u2013 \u201cinto shadow-eaten Spectres\u201d should be capitalized \u201cShadow-Eaten\u201d<br /> p 28, first para of first column \u2013 \u201cpull of the void\u201d could be capital \u201cthe Void\u201d to match?<br /> p 28, last para of first column (before sidebar) \u2013 \u201cexploring the great river\u201d might be better as capitalized \u201cGreat River\u201d I think\u2026<br /> p 28, last full para of second column \u2013 \u201cwho still had fetters\u201d should be capital \u201cFetters\u201d<br /> p 30, last full para of first column \u2013 \u201cmete out judgment and to decide\u201d needs a comma, \u201cjudgment, and to decide\u201d<br /> p 31, first full para of first column \u2013 \u201cIberia and Egypt\u201d needs a comma, \u201cIberia, and Egypt\u201d<br /> p 31, first full para of second column (after sidebar) \u2013 \u201cdestruction, hatred and the siren call\u201d needs a comma, \u201chatred, and the siren call\u201d<br /> p 31, last full para of second column \u2013 \u201cto defend Stygia and the Ferrymen took up arms\u201d needs a comma between independent clauses, \u201cdefend Stygia, and the Ferrymen\u201d<br /> p 34, fourth para of first column \u2013 \u201cwraiths called thralls\u201d should be capital \u201cThralls\u201d I think\u2026<br /> p 34, last full para of second column (before sidebar) \u2013 \u201centered the Land of the Dead\u201d uses a capitalization that does not appear the same way before this\u2026 \u201cland of the dead\u201d fits better<br /> p 35, first full para of first column \u2013 \u201cthreat to himself and his hierarchy\u201d could be capitalized \u201cHierarchy\u201d since it is referring to THE Hierarchy, right?<br /> p 35, first para of second column \u2013 \u201cthose in their care and no longer standing against Oblivion\u201d needs a comma, \u201cin their care, and no longer standing\u201d<br /> p 37, last para of second column \u2013 \u201cHeretic, Renegade and whatever foul trash\u201d needs a comma, \u201cRenegade, and whatever\u201d<br /> p 39, last para of second column \u2013 \u201con the working class and destruction\u201d needs a comma, \u201cworking class, and destruction\u201d<br /> p 40, first full para of first column \u2013 \u201cand any other that would\u201d should be plural \u201cothers\u201d<br /> p 40, first full para of second column \u2013 \u201cto the great City\u201d needs to be EITHER \u201cGreat City\u201d OR \u201cgreat city\u201d<br /> p 41, last para of first column \u2013 \u201cchallenged the Malfean and attacked\u201d needs a comma, \u201cMalfean, and attacked\u201d<br /> p 42, last para of first column \u2013 \u201camoral reapers called Harvesters\u201d should be capital \u201cReapers\u201d<br /> p 44, first para of first column \u2013 \u201cdelicately crafting ring\u201d needs to be \u201ccrafted\u201d (BUT I looooove this imagery!)<br /> p 44, second full para of second column \u2013 \u201crelics and Artifacts\u201d needs capital \u201cRelics\u201d since it\u2019s the start of a sentence<br /> p 44, last para of second column \u2013 \u201csoulforged items, It is\u201d needs lower case \u201cit\u201d<br /> p 47, last para of first column \u2013 \u201cis that thralls are souls\u201d should be capital \u201cThralls\u201d<br /> \u2026same \u2013 \u201cthen sell as thralls\u201d should be \u201cThralls\u201d<br /> p 47, last para of first column \u2013 \u201cinto a thrall\u201d should be \u201cThrall\u201d<br /> p 47, first para of second column (after sidebar) \u2013 \u201cthralls are picked\u201d should be \u201cThralls\u201d<br /> p 47, first full para of second 